          "response": {
            "result": "[sourdough-starter.md]\n# Sourdough Starter\n\nThe starter (nicknamed \"Clarence\") lives on the kitchen counter, next\nto the aquarium, in a half-liter glass jar with a loose-fitting lid.\nIt was started from scratch in January 2024 using just flour and\nwater, no store-bought starter culture.\n\nAt room temperature, Clarence needs feeding every 12 hours, equal\nparts flour and water by weight. If it's going in the fridge for\nlonger than a few days, once a week is enough, since the cold slows\nthe yeast down. Skipping a feeding at room temperature for more than a\nday makes the starter smell sharply of acetone, a sign it's hungry,\nnot a sign it's dead.\n\nBaking day starts the night before: pull the starter, feed it, and\nwait for it to double in size (usually 4 to 6 hours) before mixing the\ndough.\n"
          }
        },
